.Dd February 3, 2026
.Dt PORT-MATROIDD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm port-matroidd
.Nd deterministic scheduler network daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Op Fl -data-dir Ar path
.Op Fl -listen Ar addr
.Op Fl -control Ar path
.Op Fl -max-frame Ar bytes
.Op Fl -tick-ms Ar ms
.Op Fl -log-format Ar fmt
.Op Fl -log-level Ar level
.Op Fl -readonly
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm runs the consensus-critical scheduler network.
It validates routing context strictly, enforces replica authority,
canonicalizes all work, and applies scheduler batches deterministically.
.Pp
If any consensus validation fails, .Nm fails closed and halts.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -config Ar path
Load configuration from .Ar path .
Default: .Pa /etc/port-matroid/port-matroid.conf .
.It Fl -data-dir Ar path
State directory holding snapshots and WAL.
Default: .Pa /var/lib/port-matroid .
.It Fl -listen Ar addr
Network listen address, e.g. .Dq 0.0.0.0:7000 or .Dq [::]:7000 .
.It Fl -control Ar path
UNIX control socket path for .Xr port-matroidctl 1 .
Default: .Pa /run/port-matroid/control.sock .
.It Fl -max-frame Ar bytes
Maximum accepted network frame size.
Frames larger than this are rejected.
Default: 1048576.
.It Fl -tick-ms Ar ms
Scheduler/network tick interval in milliseconds.
Default: 250.
.It Fl -log-format Ar fmt
Log format: .Dq text or .Dq json .
Default: json.
.It Fl -log-level Ar level
Log level: .Dq debug , .Dq info , .Dq warn , .Dq error .
Default: info.
.It Fl -readonly
Disable all state mutations (no WAL appends, no snapshot writes).
Useful for audits.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/port-matroid/port-matroid.conf
Default configuration.
.It Pa /var/lib/port-matroid/snapshots/
Periodic snapshots.
.It Pa /var/lib/port-matroid/wal/
Write-ahead log segments.
.It Pa /var/lib/port-matroid/manifest
Manifest pointer to active snapshot and WAL.
.It Pa /run/port-matroid/control.sock
Control socket.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr port-matroidctl 1 ,
.Xr port-matroid.conf 5
.Sh NOTES
Consensus-critical behavior is defined by frozen specifications in the source tree.
Any divergence is a protocol fork.
